  "finalMessage": "I wrote `LabItemEditTest.kt`. I haven't run it, because it can't compile until the core lane adds `applyLabItemEdit` and `LabItemEdit`.\n\n**Files changed:** only `app/src/test/java/com/sherifradwan/ancnative/model/codex/LabItemEditTest.kt` (new). I left `check_r4c.py` and `.agents/TEST_MANIFEST.json` as they were; neither needed a fix.\n\n**`check_r4c.py` run today:** all three checks FAIL on the current code, as the brief requires.\n- **S130:** `applyLabItemEdit` is not defined anywhere, and `updateLabCodexItem` is missing from the interface and the repository.\n- **S131:** there is no `editLabCodexBtn-` tag, and settings never calls `updateLabCodexItem`.\n- **S132:** the old \"Codex\" wording is still in the visible strings, for example \"Laboratory Codex Directory\" and \"Clinic Settings, Codex & Security\". The old testTags are all still present.\n\n**Unit test, per oracle:**\n- **Q220:** nine tests call the real `applyLabItemEdit`; none copies production logic.\n  - A rename updates the item and the group entries, matching case-insensitively.\n  - Groups the rename doesn't touch stay unchanged.\n  - Changing the unit or range keeps the id and position.\n  - A blank name, an unknown id, or a name used by another item returns null.\n  - Changing only the case of the item's own name is allowed.\n  - All values are trimmed, and `isCustom` becomes true.\n- **Q221–Q223:** the unit test doesn't cover the repository wrapper, the dialog or the wording. The static checks cover those. The `UNIT-r4c` manifest entry lists them under `covers`, but this test only exercises `applyLabItemEdit` (Q220).\n\n**Assumption:** a rename keeps the group order and replaces the matching `testNames` entry in place, matching the spec's \"order kept\".",
